SAT_CHUNK("rw/form-structure/3/0",[
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.267dc2277a","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-66","passage":"<p>The architect's plan for the new library, praised by critics for its bold design, ______ a rooftop garden.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["including","to include","includes","having included"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Check the verb form: the sentence needs a main verb for \"plan\". The correct choice is “includes.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.27aea874c1","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-69","passage":"<p>A small group of residents, concerned about the plan to close the library, ______ a petition.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["having organized","organized","to organize","organizing"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Check the verb form: the sentence needs a main verb for \"group\". The correct choice is “organized.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.6c79c3e396","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-116","passage":"<p>Having studied the ancient tablets for more than a decade, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the researcher finally deciphered their meaning","the tablets' meaning was finally deciphered by the researcher","the meaning of the tablets finally became clear to the researcher","deciphering the tablets' meaning finally happened"],"answer":"A","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the researcher, so \"the researcher\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the researcher finally deciphered their meaning.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.380f651509","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-117","passage":"<p>Walking along the beach at sunrise, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Leah spotted a pod of dolphins","the dolphins swam close to Leah","the sunrise revealed a pod of dolphins to Leah","a pod of dolphins was spotted by Leah"],"answer":"A","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is Leah, so \"Leah\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “Leah spotted a pod of dolphins.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.ecedc310ac","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-118","passage":"<p>Built in 1889, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["people once thought the tower was the tallest structure in the world","the tower was once the tallest structure in the world","many visitors consider the tower the city's symbol","engineers once called the tower an impossible project"],"answer":"B","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the tower (it was built), so \"the tower\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the tower was once the tallest structure in the world.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.9ab83a2a13","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-119","passage":"<p>After finishing her homework, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["soccer was Priya's reward","the soccer game was waiting for Priya","Priya's friends invited her to play soccer","Priya went outside to play soccer"],"answer":"D","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is Priya, so \"Priya\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “Priya went outside to play soccer.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.b9a610f5fc","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-120","passage":"<p>Known for its colorful murals, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the photographers love the neighborhood","many photographers visit the neighborhood","photographers are attracted to the neighborhood","the neighborhood attracts many photographers"],"answer":"D","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the neighborhood (it is known for its murals), so \"the neighborhood\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the neighborhood attracts many photographers.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.811c312495","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-121","passage":"<p>Determined to finish the race, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the runner ignored the pain in her ankle","the pain in the runner's ankle was ignored","the runner's ankle hurt but was ignored","ignoring the pain was the runner's choice"],"answer":"A","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the runner, so \"the runner\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the runner ignored the pain in her ankle.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.21f551f237","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-122","passage":"<p>Covered in snow, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["visitors thought the mountain village looked like a postcard","the postcard scene was the mountain village","the mountain village looked like a scene from a postcard","we thought the mountain village looked like a postcard"],"answer":"C","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the village (it was covered in snow), so \"the mountain village\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the mountain village looked like a scene from a postcard.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.c480146644","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-123","passage":"<p>Using a powerful telescope, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the astronomers identified a new moon","a new moon was identified by the astronomers","the new moon became visible to the astronomers","the discovery of a new moon was made"],"answer":"A","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the astronomers, so \"the astronomers\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the astronomers identified a new moon.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.b92c49075d","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-124","passage":"<p>Originally designed as a train station, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["visitors now see art in the building","an art museum now occupies the building","the building now houses an art museum","the art museum is now in the building"],"answer":"C","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the building (it was designed as a train station), so \"the building\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the building now houses an art museum.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.594e6b54cf","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-125","passage":"<p>Excited by the results, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the experiment was repeated by the researchers","repeating the experiment was the researchers' next step","the results led the researchers to repeat the experiment","the researchers repeated the experiment"],"answer":"D","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the researchers, so \"the researchers\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the researchers repeated the experiment.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.81e99f4d09","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-137","passage":"<p>The paintings in the east gallery, many of which were donated by local families, ______ scenes from the town's past.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["has depicted","is depicting","depict","depicts"],"answer":"C","explanation":"A verb must agree in number with its subject. Here the subject is the plural noun \"paintings\"; words between the subject and the verb don't change it. The correct choice is “depict.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.7beea55e5e","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-199","passage":"<p>Stunned by the view from the summit, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the view left the climbers silent","the climbers stood silently for several minutes","silence fell over the climbers for several minutes","several minutes passed in silence for the climbers"],"answer":"B","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the climbers (they were stunned), so \"the climbers\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the climbers stood silently for several minutes.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.abebd6bef8","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-200","passage":"<p>Having won three championships in a row, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["a fourth title seemed likely for the team","the team was favored to win again","fans expected the team to win again","the team's fans were confident of another win"],"answer":"B","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the team, so \"the team\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the team was favored to win again.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.d40c0d50ef","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-201","passage":"<p>Painted in bright shades of blue, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["visitors can easily spot the house","the house stands out on the quiet street","the quiet street is brightened by the house","neighbors notice the house on the quiet street"],"answer":"B","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the house (it was painted), so \"the house\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the house stands out on the quiet street.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.bf1227dfb3","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-202","passage":"<p>While reviewing the budget, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["errors appeared in the budget","the budget revealed several errors to the treasurer","the treasurer found several errors","several errors were found by the treasurer"],"answer":"C","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the treasurer, so \"the treasurer\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the treasurer found several errors.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.fe706ed9e8","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-203","passage":"<p>Frightened by the thunder, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the bed became the puppy's hiding place","the puppy hid under the bed","thunder made the puppy hide under the bed","hiding under the bed was the puppy's reaction"],"answer":"B","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the puppy (it was frightened), so \"the puppy\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the puppy hid under the bed.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.68653e407f","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-204","passage":"<p>To qualify for the finals, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the top eight swimmers are chosen","a swimmer must finish in the top eight","the top eight is where a swimmer must finish","finishing in the top eight is required of swimmers"],"answer":"B","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is a swimmer, so \"a swimmer\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “a swimmer must finish in the top eight.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.726e3a1c24","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-205","passage":"<p>Located at the edge of the desert, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["residents rely on water piped from the mountains","the town depends on water piped from the mountains","water must be piped to the town from the mountains","the mountains supply the town with water"],"answer":"B","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is the town (it is located at the edge of the desert), so \"the town\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “the town depends on water piped from the mountains.”"},
{"id":"g.rw.form-structure.3.0d183c3ffd","section":"rw","domain":"conventions","skill":"form-structure","difficulty":3,"group":"form-206","passage":"<p>Unable to find her keys, ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Keiko searched every pocket of her coat","every pocket of Keiko's coat was searched","the keys were nowhere in Keiko's coat","Keiko's coat pockets were searched one by one"],"answer":"A","explanation":"An introductory modifier must be followed immediately by the person or thing it describes, which here is Keiko, so \"Keiko\" must come right after the opening phrase. The correct choice is “Keiko searched every pocket of her coat.”"}
]);
